{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Strange Stories From the Hospital", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Good Service", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 11, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Inseparable Phrasal Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Phrasal verbs are two-part verbs consisting of a verb followed by an adverb particle (these look like prepositions, but do not have the same function in phrasal verbs).<br/><br/> In some cases, it is not possible to separate the verb and the particle. These are called <span class=\"italic\">inseparable</span> phrasal verbs.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "It is important to remember that the meaning of a phrasal verb is often very different from the two parts taken separately.<br/><br/> For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Matt <span class=\"strong\">turned up</span> last night</span> (= appeared, not the same as turned + up).<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">To turn up</span> is an inseparable phrasal verb. You cannot put an object between the verb and the particle. It must remain together. <br/><br/> Another example is <span class=\"italic\">to get off</span>. <br/> You can say \u201c<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">get off</span> the bus</span>\u201d, but you cannot say \u201c<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">get</span> the bus <span class=\"strong\">off</span></span>\u201d.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "A few verbs can be used with both a particle and a preposition, making them <span class=\"strong\">three-part verbs</span>.<br/><br/> For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">to run away with</span> (to leave; to escape from)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">to watch out for</span> (to be careful for)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">to back out of</span> (to fail to keep a promise)<br/><br/>  Learning phrasal verbs is a lot like learning new vocabulary. You must memorize which phrasal verbs are inseparable and learn their meanings. <br/><br/>  Look at the chart for some more inseparable phrasal verbs and their meanings.<br/> <br/>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Phrasal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Meaning</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">stand up to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"support; defend\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">tell on\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"report misbehavior\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">look for\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"find\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">go up to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"approach\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I went up to the counter.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The girl was looking for something in her purse.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "As far as I'm concerned, you should tell on them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Stand up for our rights as consumers. <br/> <br/>", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Simple Past and The Past Continuous Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You often use the Simple Past and the Past Continuous tenses together.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the Past Continuous tense to refer to the context of a story. It talks about the \u2018background' action, or the longer action. You use it to talk about an action that was in progress in the past.<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">The older man <span class=\"strong\">was drinking</span> a cup of coffee.</span> <br/><br/>  You can use the Simple Past tense to refer to a shorter action that happened in the middle of, or interrupted, the longer action.<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Yesterday I <span class=\"strong\">went</span> to my local health clinic to make an appointment. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The girl behind the counter was talking on the telephone.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The young woman was filing her nails.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The older man was reading a magazine.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The efficient-looking matron was staring into space.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Obviously the clerks weren't working, and I was really annoyed. ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to motion", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to move your hand or head in order to indicate something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She motioned for me to sit down. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about customer service in a health clinic.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to file", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to rub a metal or wooden tool against the surface of an object to make it smoother", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The young woman was filing her nails.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to stare into space", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to look somewhere for a long time without actually seeing anything particular because you are thinking of something else", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The efficient-looking matron was staring into space. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to assert", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to express your opinion firmly and with conviction", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Finally, I decided to assert myself.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to stand up for", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to defend; especially when criticized or attacked", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You should stand up for our rights as consumers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to stand up to", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to not permit anyone to treat you badly ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We need to stand up to the customer service!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to tell on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to report to someone what somebody has done badly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You should tell on the clerks and express your concern.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Talk about a time that you were not happy with the service you received.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Explain what happened and what you think about the situation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a letter of complaint to the person/people you think were responsible.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Explain what you would like them to do to rectify the problem.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your letter to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I explain what happened and express my opinion about a situation in which I received bad service.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a letter complaining about the experience.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain how the problem could be solved.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my letter.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about common health problems.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about what was happening when something else happened. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can explain my opinion.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " How is the customer service in your country?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Do you believe that the \u201ccustomer is always right\u201d? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "What terrible customer service!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "id": 0, "type": "WLC"}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "_data": [{"contents"